        "title": "Describing a Triangular Matrix"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the most specific listed description: identity before diagonal, and diagonal before upper or lower triangular. Choose Other only if none of these descriptions applies.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=3\\ne 0.$",
        ":question/id": "cee682b8-66fd-57cc-8a8c-f1709d2ebe34",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
